{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Weekly Status Update",
  "description": "Drafts weekly status updates for the current user's tasks in a project management tool, presents them for approval, and writes approved updates back. Asks which sprint/iteration and task scope before proceeding.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are running the weekly status update workflow.\n\n## Configuration\n\nBefore using this hook, configure these values for your team:\n- Room/Project ID: [YOUR_PROJECT_ID]\n- Project name: [YOUR_PROJECT_NAME]\n- PM tool: [Taskei / Jira / Linear / Asana / Notion]\n\n## Step 0: Gather Runtime Parameters\n\nALWAYS ask the user for these at the start of every run. Do NOT reuse values from previous runs.\n\n### 0a. Identity\nAsk for the user's username/alias. Confirm it back to them.\n\n### 0b. Sprint/Iteration selection\nFetch available sprints/iterations from the project management tool. Present the list with names and IDs. Ask the user which one they want to update. Do NOT guess or default — always ask and confirm.\n\n### 0c. Task scope\nAsk which tasks to include:\n- (1) 'Assigned to me' — tasks where the user is the assignee\n- (2) 'Created by me' — tasks where the user is the creator\n- (3) 'Both' — union of the two (deduplicated)\n\nDefault to (1) if not specified. Confirm before proceeding.\n\n## Step 1: Fetch Tasks\n\nBased on scope chosen in Step 0c, fetch:\n- Open tasks in the selected sprint\n- Open tasks without a sprint (backlog/carryover)\n- Recently closed tasks (last 7 days) in the selected sprint\n\n## Step 2: Get Task Details\n\nFor each task, retrieve:\n- Status/workflow step\n- Any existing weekly update or status field\n- Recent comments (last 10)\n- Blocked status and reason\n- Assignee, creator, estimate\n\n## Step 3: Gather Context\n\nReview chat history, code activity, and task comments to understand what happened this week.\n\n## Step 4: Draft Status Updates\n\nDraft an update per task in this format:\n\n```\n<M/D>:\n- Concise action-oriented bullet about what was done\n- Another bullet about progress or decisions\n- Use FULL NAMES of people involved (never @handles)\n- Factual, no fluff\n\nRisks/Dependencies:\n- Only include if there are actual blockers or risks\n```\n\nStyle rules:\n- Date prefix in M/D format (e.g., 5/7)\n- Use '-' bullets only (never '*' or numbered lists)\n- FULL NAMES only, never @alias (aliases may not render in reports/newsletters)\n- Plain text, avoid em dashes\n- 'Risks/Dependencies:' section only when actual blockers exist\n- Prepend new entries to existing status (newest on top)\n- For tasks closed within last 7 days, include 'CLOSED' in the update\n- Do NOT add updates to tasks closed more than 7 days ago\n\n## Step 5: Flag Unknown Tasks\n\nFor tasks with no context, no recent comments, no activity:\n- Flag with [!] NO CONTEXT\n- Show title, status, last update date\n- Ask the user for status\n- Do NOT fabricate status\n\n## Step 6: Present for Approval\n\nShow all drafts. For each task include:\n- Task ID and title\n- Scope tag (if scope=Both): [Assigned], [Created], or [Both]\n- Current status/workflow step\n- Sprint assignment\n- Existing status update (abbreviated)\n- Proposed new update to prepend\n- [!] flag if no context\n\nAsk the user to:\n- Approve all / approve specific IDs\n- Reject with corrections\n- Provide status for [!] tasks\n- Skip specific tasks\n\n## Step 7: Write to PM Tool (ONLY after explicit approval)\n\nFor each approved update:\n- Update the status/weekly update field — prepend new content\n- Write sequentially (not in parallel) to avoid rate limits or byte-limit errors\n- If a write fails due to size: trim older entries (keep most recent 2-3 dated entries) and retry\n\nConfirm each write with task ID and link.\n\n## Important Reminders\n\n1. ALWAYS ask for sprint at the start — never assume\n2. ALWAYS ask for task scope — default to 'assigned' only if user explicitly skips\n3. NEVER use @alias format — full names only\n4. NEVER fabricate status for unknown tasks — ask the user\n5. After writing, verify each task's status field to confirm content saved"
  }
}
